          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            may be thought of as a “locally linear space”: a space that is locally isomorphic to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            In the broader context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            there may exist
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            — in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            with line object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            — considerably more general than manifolds. While for all of them there is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X : = X^D
            (sometimes called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+tangent+bundle"} synthetic tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal interval
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            A
            %em microlinear space
            is essentially an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            does have
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            In fact the definition is a bit stronger than that, but the main point in practice of microlinearity is that the linearity of the fibers of the tangent bundle allows to apply most of the familiar constructions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            to these spaces.
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (microlinear space)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
              with line object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{T}
              is a
              %strong microlinear space
              if for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta : J \to \mathcal{T}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+spaces"} infinitesimal spaces
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              and for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} cocone
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \to \Delta_c
              under it such that homming into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              produces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              diagram ,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi R
                        %mi c
                        %mi Δ
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi lim
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\Delta_c \simeq \lim_{j \in J} R^{\Delta_j}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              produces a limit diagram:
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi X
                        %mi c
                        %mi Δ
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi lim
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\Delta_c \simeq \lim_{j \in J} X^{\Delta_j}
          %p The main point of this definition is the following property.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (fiberwise linearity of tangent bundle)
            %p
              For every microlinear space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^D \to X
              has a natural fiberwise
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "-structure." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
          .proof
            %h6#construction_and_proof Construction and Proof
            %p
              We describe first the addition of tangent vectors, then the
              = succeed "-action" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "-structure." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %strong Addition
                  With
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msup
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \coloneqq \{\epsilon \in R| \epsilon^2 = 0 \}
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal interval
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi R
                        %mo ×
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(2) \coloneqq \big\{(\epsilon_1, \epsilon_2) \in R \times R | \epsilon_i \epsilon_j = 0\big\}
                  we have a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi D
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ←
                              %mtd
                                %mi D
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi D
                              %mtd
                                %mo ←
                              %mtd
                                %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        D(2) &amp;\leftarrow&amp; D
                        \\\
                        \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                        \\\
                        D &amp;\leftarrow&amp; {*}
                        }
                %p such that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi R
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi D
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi R
                                  %mi D
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi R
                                  %mi D
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        R^{D(2)} &amp;\to &amp; R^D
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        R^D &amp;\to&amp; R
                        }
                %p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kock-Lawvere+axiom"} Kock-Lawvere axiom
                  satisfied in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is microlinear, also the canonical map
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        r \;\colon\; X^{D(2)} \to X^D \times_X X^D
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Id
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Id
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Id \times Id \colon D \to D(2)
                  the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+map"} diagonal map
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/addition"} addition
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^D \times_X X^D \to X^D
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^D
                  to be given by the map
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi r
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi Id
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Id
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        + \;\colon\; X^D \times_X X^D \stackrel{r^{-1}}{\to} X^{D(2)} \stackrel{X^{Id \times Id}}{\to}
                        X^D
                        \\,.
                %p
                  On elements, this sends a pair
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1, v_2 \in X^D
                  in the same fiber to the element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1 + v_2
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^D
                  given by the map
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 2
